pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2477074</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><citation citation-type="journal">Demo, S.D., and G. Yellen. <year>1991</year>. The inactivation gate of the <italic>Shaker</italic> K<sup>&#x0002b;</sup> channel behaves like an open-channel blocker. <source>Neuron.</source> <volume>7</volume>:<fpage>743</fpage>&#x02013;753.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1742023</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><citation citation-type="journal">Demo, S.D., and G. Yellen. <year>1992</year>. Ion effects on gating of the Ca<sup>2&#x0002b;</sup>-activated K<sup>&#x0002b;</sup> channel correlate with occupancy of the pore. <source>Biophys. J.</source> <volume>61</volume>:<fpage>639</fpage>&#x02013;648.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1504240</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><citation citation-type="journal">Doyle, D.A., J. Morais Cabral, R.A. Pfuetzner, A. Kuo, J.M. Gulbis, S.L. Cohen, B.T. Chait, and R. MacKinnon. <year>1998</year>. The structure of the potassium channel: molecular basis of K<sup>&#x0002b;</sup> conduction and selectivity. <source>Science.</source> <volume>280</volume>:<fpage>69</fpage>&#x02013;77.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9525859</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib22"><citation citation-type="journal">Gao, L., X. Mi, V. Paajanen, K. Wang, and Z. Fan. <year>2005</year>. Activation-coupled inactivation in the bacterial potassium channel KcsA. <source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA.</source> <volume>102</volume>:<fpage>17630</fpage>&#x02013;17635.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16301524</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib23"><citation citation-type="journal">Gonoi, T., and B. Hille. <year>1987</year>. Gating of Na channels. Inactivation modifiers discriminate among models. <source>J. Gen. Physiol.</source> <volume>89</volume>:<fpage>253</fpage>&#x02013;274.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2435840</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib24"><citation citation-type="journal">Gross, A., L. Columbus, K. Hideg, C. Altenbach, and W.L. Hubbell. <year>1999</year>. Structure of the KcsA potassium channel from <italic>Streptomyces lividans</italic>: a site directed spin labeling study of the second transmembrane segment. <source>Biochemistry.</source> <volume>38</volume>:<fpage>10324</fpage>&#x02013;10335.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10441126</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib25"><citation citation-type="journal">Heginbotham, L., L. Kolmakova-Partensky, and C. Miller. <year>1998</year>. Functional reconstitution of a prokaryotic K<sup>&#x0002b;</sup> channel. <source>J. Gen. Physiol.</source> <volume>111</volume>:<fpage>741</fpage>&#x02013;749.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9607934</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib26"><citation citation-type="journal">Heginbotham, L., M. LeMasurier, L. Kolmakova-Partensky, and C. Miller. <year>1999</year>. Single <italic>Streptomyces lividans</italic> K<sup>&#x0002b;</sup> channels: functional asymmetries and sidedness of proton activation. <source>J. Gen. Physiol.</source> <volume>114</volume>:<fpage>551</fpage>&#x02013;560.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10498673</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib27"><citation citation-type="journal">Hoshi, T., W.N. Zagotta, and R.W. Aldrich. <year>1994</year>. Shaker potassium channel gating. I: Transitions near the open state. <source>J. Gen. Physiol.</source> <volume>103</volume>:<fpage>249</fpage>&#x02013;278.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8189206</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib28"><citation citation-type="journal">Irizarry, S.N., E. Kutluay, G. Drews, S.J. Hart, and L. Heginbotham. <year>2002</year>. Opening the KcsA K<sup>&#x0002b;</sup> channel: tryptophan scanning and complementation analysis lead to mutants with altered gating. <source>Biochemistry.</source> <volume>41</volume>:<fpage>13653</fpage>&#x02013;13662.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12427027</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib29"><citation citation-type="journal">Jiang, Y., A. Lee, J. Chen, M. Cadene, B.T. Chait, and R. MacKinnon. <year>2002</year>. Crystal structure and mechanism of a ca